   <collaboration id="Collaboration_c1630ef6-f014-4269-a960-ef69fb09e8c9"
                   name="CSP-BPMN-L2-003 - Process Daily Valuation"
                   isClosed="false">
      <documentation><![CDATA[Traceability: CSP-PR-003; CSP-VL-001-006; SCN-005.
 
Purpose:  Represent the assumed current-state operational processing of scheduled daily valuations for FX Forward positions.
 
The process begins when the daily valuation cycle is triggered and SYS-VAL produces the scheduled valuation file. It covers file-level controls, comparison of the valuation population with active positions in SYS-FAP and the operational lifecycle tracker, identification of normal and exception populations, manual preparation and submission of accepted valuations to SYS-FAP, reconciliation of processing results, confirmation of the applied valuation state, and review of the resulting accounting and NAV impact.
 
The process end with either confirmed successful daily valuation processing or a documented unsuccessful exception outcome with a recorded status, assigned owner, supporting evidence, and required next action.
 
Market-data sourcing, internal valuation-model calculation, detailed FAP ledger logic, internal NAV calculation and publication, SYS-INT, target-state orchestration, APIs, canonical messages, and automated retry capabilities are outside scope.
 
Evidence status: Current-state case-study assumption.]]></documentation>
