Input: Valuation records separated from the accepted population by record-level and population controls.
 
Handling: Investigate and classify missing, stale, duplicate, rejected, unknown-trade and historical-version valuations. Preserve the relevant trade, version, valuation-date and source identifiers and determine the responsible owner and required corrective action.
 
Output: Classified valuation exception population and the corresponding correction, replacement or escalation requirement.]]></documentation>
